# The Emergence of Social Cognitive Neuroscience.

**Authors:** Ochsner, Kevin N., Lieberman, Matthew D.

## Abstract
New research methods have spawned social cognitive neuroscience. Social and emotional phenomena can now be studied at three levels. The study of neural mechanisms, cognitions, and social processes is integrated by interdisciplinary research endeavors, yielding new knowledge about stereotyping, attitude change, and how human beings process certain emotionally charged events. (Author/SM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ634006

